{%- doc -%}
  Renders the collection grid entry for one product: one card per variant option value
  when the section's "Split variants into separate cards" setting is on, otherwise the
  single card the theme has always rendered.

  Which option splits: the first one that is not a size axis. Size stays collapsed inside
  a card (a ring lists once per metal, not once per metal per size), and 'Title' is
  Shopify's placeholder option on single-variant products, so it is skipped too.
  Everything else — Metal color, Silk color — becomes its own card.

  The representative variant per value comes from `option_value.variant`, the same source
  product-grid-item already uses for its swatch images (line ~244). That avoids looping
  product.variants, which Liquid caps at 50 iterations per loop.

  No product in the catalogue has more than one non-size option, so a single split axis
  covers all of them; if that ever changes, only the first non-size option splits.

  @param {product} product - The product to render
  @param {boolean} [split_variants] - Section setting; false renders one card per product
  @param {number} [index] - Position in the grid loop
  @param {string} [sizes] - Image sizes attribute
  @param {string} [attributes] - Extra html attributes for the card
  @param {number} [animation_delay] - Stagger for the entrance animation
  @param {string} [card_animation] - Animation flavour ('plp' on collection pages)

  @example
  {% render 'collection-grid-cards', product: product, split_variants: section.settings.collection_split_variants, index: forloop.index, sizes: image_sizes, card_animation: 'plp' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign split_option = blank

  if split_variants
    # size axes stay inside the card; 'title' is Shopify's placeholder option
    assign size_option_names = 'size,title' | split: ','

    for option in product.options_with_values
      assign option_key = option.name | downcase | strip
      unless size_option_names contains option_key
        assign split_option = option
        break
      endunless
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- if split_option == blank -%}
  {%- render 'product-grid-item',
    product: product,
    index: index,
    sizes: sizes,
    attributes: attributes,
    animation_delay: animation_delay,
    card_animation: card_animation
  -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- for option_value in split_option.values -%}
    {%- render 'product-grid-item',
      product: product,
      variant: option_value.variant,
      index: index,
      sizes: sizes,
      attributes: attributes,
      animation_delay: animation_delay,
      card_animation: card_animation
    -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
